The map's land and the images this plugin shows are not covered by this
plugin's licence. The plugin always shows, with a satellite image, the
satellite, the time of the image and the agency's credit, word for word as
its terms give it. It uses no
agency's logo, and Kiosko and this plugin are not affiliated with, nor
endorsed by, any of them.

Natural Earth
  src/land-data.ts is derived from Natural Earth's 1:50m land polygons
  (ne_50m_land), simplified. Natural Earth is in the public domain.
  Made with Natural Earth. Free vector and raster map data @
  naturalearthdata.com.

NOAA/NESDIS/STAR, GOES-East (GOES-19) and GOES-West (GOES-18)
  GeoColor full-disk images from https://cdn.star.nesdis.noaa.gov (no key).
  Works of the US federal government: public domain. GeoColor imagery is
  produced by CIRA (Cooperative Institute for Research in the Atmosphere,
  Colorado State University) with NOAA/NESDIS/STAR.
  https://www.star.nesdis.noaa.gov/GOES/
  Shown as: "NOAA/NESDIS/STAR, CIRA · public domain".
  The screenshots in docs/ show GOES-19 images (public domain).

Japan Meteorological Agency, Himawari-9
  True Color Reproduction full-disk images from the Meteorological
  Satellite Center's real-time page, https://www.data.jma.go.jp/mscweb/data/himawari/
  (no key). Under the terms of use of the JMA website (Public Data License
  1.0, compatible with Creative Commons Attribution 4.0):
  "Source: Japan Meteorological Agency website". True Color Reproduction
  imagery was developed by the JMA Meteorological Satellite Center with the
  NOAA/NESDIS/STAR GOES-R Algorithm Working Group imagery team, using
  software from CIRA; its terms ask to credit the Japan Meteorological
  Agency (JMA), NOAA/NESDIS and Colorado State University–CIRA (CSU/CIRA).
  The plugin resizes the images and cuts them to the Earth's disk.
  https://www.jma.go.jp/jma/en/copyright.html
  https://www.jma.go.jp/jma/jma-eng/satellite/introduction/TCR.html
  Shown, whole (in turns on small tiles), as: "Source: Japan Meteorological
  Agency website (https://www.data.jma.go.jp/mscweb/data/himawari/), resized
  and cropped · True Color Reproduction: JMA, NOAA/NESDIS, CSU/CIRA".

EUMETSAT, Meteosat-12 (0°) and Meteosat-9 (45.5°E, Indian Ocean)
  GeoColour and Natural Colour Enhanced RGB images from the EUMETView map
  service, https://view.eumetsat.int (WMS, no key). Under EUMETSAT's Data
  Policy, RGB images and other visualisations are Advanced Image Products,
  "Core" data available on a free and unrestricted basis under CC BY 4.0,
  with the attribution "[Contains modified] EUMETSAT [Meteosat]
  [data/product] [year]". The plugin reprojects them from latitude and
  longitude to the satellite's view of the Earth.
  https://www.eumetsat.int/data-policy
  Shown, whole (in turns on small tiles), as: "Contains modified EUMETSAT
  Meteosat data <year> · CC BY 4.0".

Test fixtures
  src/fixtures/jma-fd.html is an excerpt of the JMA real-time page (its list
  of image times), src/fixtures/eumetview-mtg-geocolour-caps.xml a layer's
  capabilities from EUMETView, both as served on 2026-11-27, under the terms
  above. src/fixtures/astro-ref.json holds positions computed with astropy
  (scripts/ref_astropy.py).
